"A bag?" the shop assistant asks.
"No thank you," I say.
I do not need a bag.
I put the new clothes on right away.
First, I put on the thick, red sweater.
Then, I put on the dark-blue winter jacket.
I zip the warm jacket.
Afterwards, I take the long, blue scarf.
I wrap it around my neck.
Finally, I put on the new, black gloves.
Now I have all my warm clothes on.
I smile and say goodbye.
I walk out of the shop.
I stand out on the cold street again.
It is freezing cold.
The wind blows hard.
But I am not freezing at all.
Now I am ready for winter.
